  "worked_solution": "The elements of the given set are the natural numbers that satisfy the inequality $24<4n.$ \n\nSo, we first need to solve our inequality for $n:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}24 & <4n \\\\ 6 & <n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe positive integer solutions of the inequality above are $7,8,9,10,11,12,\u2026.$ Therefore, the given set can be written as \n\n$$\nC={7,8,9,10,11,12,\u2026}.\n$$",
